== the answer to a create is lost; the owner restarts
  A after the failed push: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight; entries on the main: 1
  restarted, then a write to the same name: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="two"; position 2, 0 pending; entries: 2
  B: f="two"

== a create that never left; the owner restarts
  A after the failed push: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight; entries on the main: 0
  restarted: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="one"; position 1, 0 pending; entries: 1

== an arrival record left by a crash is completed at start
  B after its start, with no cycle: f="again"  g="new"; position 2, 0 pending
  an anchor from before the crash: stale: the frontend lists again
  the next cycle: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending

== a push refused by a commit that touches nothing pending
  B: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  chunks B sent after A's commit got ahead: 0; entries: 2
  B: mine="from B"  theirs="from A"
  A: mine="from B"  theirs="from A"

== more commands than an entry holds
  A: 0 entries merged, 3 committed, 0 pending
  commands per entry: 256, 256, 88; tree head: 3
  B holds 600 links

== a file renamed, then edited, while its upload is held
  A: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 2 pending
  B meanwhile: f="kept"
  once the upload passes, A: position 2, 0 pending
  B: g="EDIT"

== an entry no client can decode, then voided
  A: failed: log entry 2 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]
  A: position 1, 1 pending, cannot follow entry 2 (it does not decode: expected a JSON object)
  B: failed: log entry 2 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]; position 1, 0 pending, cannot follow entry 2 (it does not decode: expected a JSON object)
  voided. A: 1 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending
  B: 2 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending; f="one"  g="behind"
  entries: 3; tree head: 1

== an entry of a later version
  A: failed: log entry 1 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]
  A: position 0, 1 pending, cannot follow entry 1 (it is of version 2)
  a void object changes nothing for it: failed: log entry 1 cannot be followed: fetching and pushing stop until it is voided or this client is upgraded [corrupt/other]

== a chunk the main lost before the commit
  A, its create failing: position 0, 1 pending, a push in flight
  A, the chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 1 pending
  A: position 0, 1 pending
  after the upload ran again: position 1, 0 pending; entries: 1
  B: f="abcdefgh"

== a refused file is committed once written again
  A, renamed, a chunk gone from the main: 0 entries merged, 0 committed, 2 pending
  damaged: g
  A, g written again: position 2, 0 pending; damaged: 0
  B: g="ijkl"

== a parked copy is retried, and the pause flag is where 07 says
  the replica refusing, it holds the chunk: false
  re-armed: true; the replica holds the chunk: true
  paused, the flag exists: true

== an entry its author never projected
  A merges it without waiting for its projection: 1 entries merged, 0 committed, 0 pending
  A: f="one"  g="dead"; tree head: 1 of 2
  A commits behind it: 0 entries merged, 1 committed, 0 pending; tree head: 1 of 3
  a new client arrives by state over the unprojected entries: f="one"  g="dead"  h="after"

== a position that is gone: arrival by state keeps pending work
  B: arrived by state, 1 committed, 0 pending
  B: f="from A"  mine="from B"  shared="from A"  shared (conflicted copy from B)="from B"
  A: f="from A"  mine="from B"  shared="from A"  shared (conflicted copy from B)="from B"

